Pseudodragon ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Pseudodragon ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Pseudodragon Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.316	DESC:The pseudodragon makes two Bite attacks.
Pseudodragon ~ Bite	KEY:Creature ~ Pseudodragon ~ Bite	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Pseudodragon Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Bite	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.316	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage.
Pseudodragon ~ Sting	KEY:Creature ~ Pseudodragon ~ Sting	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Pseudodragon Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Sting	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.316	DESC:Constitution Saving Throw: DC 12, one creature the pseudodragon can see within 5 feet. Failure: 5 (2d4) Poison damage, and the target has the Poisoned condition for 1 hour. Failure by 5 or More: While Poisoned, the target also has the Unconscious condition, which ends early if the target takes damage or a creature within 5 feet of it takes an action to wake it.
Purple Worm ~ Tunneler	KEY:Creature ~ Purple Worm ~ Tunneler	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Purple Worm Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Tunneler	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.316	DESC:The worm can burrow through solid rock at half its Burrow Speed and leaves a 10-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.
Purple Worm ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Purple Worm ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Purple Worm Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.316	DESC:The worm makes one Bite attack and one Tail Stinger attack.
Purple Worm ~ Bite	KEY:Creature ~ Purple Worm ~ Bite	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Purple Worm Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Bite	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.316	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +14, reach 10 ft. Hit: 22 (3d8 + 9) Piercing damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the Grappled condition (escape DC 19), and it has the Restrained condition until the grapple ends.
Purple Worm ~ Tail Stinger	KEY:Creature ~ Purple Worm ~ Tail Stinger	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Purple Worm Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Tail Stinger	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.316	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +14, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (2d6 + 9) Piercing damage plus 35 (10d6) Poison damage.
Purple Worm ~ Swallow	KEY:Creature ~ Purple Worm ~ Swallow	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Purple Worm Trait.MonsterBonusAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Swallow	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.316	DESC:Strength Saving Throw: DC 19, one Large or smaller creature Grappled by the worm (it can have up to three creatures swallowed at a time). Failure: The target is swallowed by the worm, and the Grappled condition ends. A swallowed creature has the Blinded and Restrained conditions, has Total Cover against attacks and other effects outside the worm, and takes 17 (5d6) Acid damage at the start of each of the worm’s turns. If the worm takes 30 damage or more on a single turn from a creature inside it, the worm must succeed on a DC 21 Constitution saving throw at the end of that turn or regurgitate all swallowed creatures, each of which falls in a space within 5 feet of the worm and has the Prone condition. If the worm dies, any swallowed creature no longer has the Restrained condition and can escape from the corpse using 20 feet of movement, exiting Prone.
Quasit ~ Magic Resistance	KEY:Creature ~ Quasit ~ Magic Resistance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Quasit Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Magic Resistance	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.317	DESC:The quasit has Advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.
Quasit ~ Rend	KEY:Creature ~ Quasit ~ Rend	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Quasit Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Rend	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.317	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Slashing damage, and the target has the Poisoned condition until the start of the quasit’s next turn.
Quasit ~ Invisibility	KEY:Creature ~ Quasit ~ Invisibility	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Quasit Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Invisibility	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.317	DESC:The quasit casts Invisibility on itself, requiring no spell components and using Charisma as the spellcasting ability.
Quasit ~ Scare (1/Day)	KEY:Creature ~ Quasit ~ Scare (1/Day)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Quasit Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Scare (1/Day)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.317	DESC:Wisdom Saving Throw: DC 10, one creature within 20 feet. Failure: The target has the Frightened condition. At the end of each of its turns, the target repeats the save, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically.
Quasit ~ Shape-Shift	KEY:Creature ~ Quasit ~ Shape-Shift	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Quasit Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Shape-Shift	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.317	DESC:The quasit shape-shifts to resemble a bat (Speed 10 ft., Fly 40 ft.), a centipede (40 ft., Climb 40 ft.), or a toad (40 ft., Swim 40 ft.), or it returns to its true form. Its game statistics are the same in each form, except for its Speed. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn’t transformed.
Rakshasa ~ Greater Magic Resistance	KEY:Creature ~ Rakshasa ~ Greater Magic Resistance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Rakshasa Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Greater Magic Resistance	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.317	DESC:The rakshasa automatically succeeds on saving throws against spells and other magical effects, and the attack rolls of spells automatically miss it. Without the rakshasa’s permission, no spell can observe the rakshasa remotely or detect its thoughts, creature type, or alignment.
Rakshasa ~ Fiendish Restoration	KEY:Creature ~ Rakshasa ~ Fiendish Restoration	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Rakshasa Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Fiendish Restoration	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.317	DESC:If the rakshasa dies outside the Nine Hells, its body turns to ichor, and it gains a new body instantly, reviving with all its Hit Points somewhere in the Nine Hells.
Rakshasa ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Rakshasa ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Rakshasa Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.317	DESC:The rakshasa makes three Cursed Touch attacks.
Rakshasa ~ Cursed Touch	KEY:Creature ~ Rakshasa ~ Cursed Touch	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Rakshasa Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Cursed Touch	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.317	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 5) Slashing damage plus 19 (3d12) Necrotic damage. If the target is a creature, it is cursed. While cursed, the target gains no benefit from finishing a Short or Long Rest.
Rakshasa ~ Baleful Command (Recharge 5–6)	KEY:Creature ~ Rakshasa ~ Baleful Command (Recharge 5–6)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Rakshasa Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Baleful Command (Recharge 5–6)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.317	DESC:Wisdom Saving Throw: DC 18, each enemy in a 30-foot Emanation originating from the rakshasa. Failure: 28 (8d6) Psychic damage, and the target has the Frightened and Incapacitated conditions until the start of the rakshasa’s next turn.
Rakshasa ~ Spellcasting	KEY:Creature ~ Rakshasa ~ Spellcasting	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Rakshasa Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Spellcasting	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.317	DESC:The rakshasa casts one of the following spells, requiring no Material components and using Charisma as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 18): At Will: Detect Magic , Detect Thoughts , Disguise Self , Mage Hand , Minor Illusion 1/Day Each: Fly , Invisibility , Major Image , Plane Shift
