Stone Giant ~ Stone Club	KEY:Creature ~ Stone Giant ~ Stone Club	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Stone Giant Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Stone Club	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.330	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 15 ft. Hit: 22 (3d10 + 6) Bludgeoning damage.
Stone Giant ~ Boulder	KEY:Creature ~ Stone Giant ~ Boulder	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Stone Giant Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Boulder	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.330	DESC:Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 60/240 ft. Hit: 15 (2d8 + 6) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the Prone condition.
Stone Giant ~ Deflect Missile (Recharge 5–6)	KEY:Creature ~ Stone Giant ~ Deflect Missile (Recharge 5–6)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Stone Giant Trait.MonsterReaction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Deflect Missile (Recharge 5–6)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.330	DESC:Trigger: The giant is hit by a ranged attack roll and takes Bludgeoning, Piercing, or Slashing damage from it. Response: The giant reduces the damage it takes from the attack by 11 (1d10 + 6), and if that damage is reduced to 0, the giant can redirect some of the attack’s force. Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 17, one creature the giant can see within 60 feet. Failure: 11 (1d10 + 6) Force damage.
Stone Golem ~ Immutable Form	KEY:Creature ~ Stone Golem ~ Immutable Form	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Stone Golem Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Immutable Form	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.330	DESC:The golem can’t shape-shift.
Stone Golem ~ Magic Resistance	KEY:Creature ~ Stone Golem ~ Magic Resistance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Stone Golem Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Magic Resistance	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.330	DESC:The golem has Advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.
Stone Golem ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Stone Golem ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Stone Golem Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.330	DESC:The golem makes two attacks, using Slam or Force Bolt in any combination.
Stone Golem ~ Slam	KEY:Creature ~ Stone Golem ~ Slam	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Stone Golem Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Slam	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.330	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (2d8 + 6) Bludgeoning damage plus 9 (2d8) Force damage.
Stone Golem ~ Force Bolt	KEY:Creature ~ Stone Golem ~ Force Bolt	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Stone Golem Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Force Bolt	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.330	DESC:Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 120 ft. Hit: 22 (4d10) Force damage.
Stone Golem ~ Slow (Recharge 5–6)	KEY:Creature ~ Stone Golem ~ Slow (Recharge 5–6)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Stone Golem Trait.MonsterBonusAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Slow (Recharge 5–6)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.330	DESC:The golem casts the Slow spell, requiring no spell components and using Constitution as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 17).
Storm Giant ~ Amphibious	KEY:Creature ~ Storm Giant ~ Amphibious	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Storm Giant Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Amphibious	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.330	DESC:The giant can breathe air and water.
Storm Giant ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Storm Giant ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Storm Giant Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.330	DESC:The giant makes two attacks, using Storm Sword or Thunderbolt in any combination.
Storm Giant ~ Storm Sword	KEY:Creature ~ Storm Giant ~ Storm Sword	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Storm Giant Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Storm Sword	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.330	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +14, reach 10 ft. Hit: 23 (4d6 + 9) Slashing damage plus 13 (3d8) Lightning damage.
Storm Giant ~ Thunderbolt	KEY:Creature ~ Storm Giant ~ Thunderbolt	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Storm Giant Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Thunderbolt	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.330	DESC:Ranged Attack Roll: +14, range 500 ft. Hit: 22 (2d12 + 9) Lightning damage, and the target has the Blinded and Deafened conditions until the start of the giant’s next turn.
Storm Giant ~ Lightning Storm (Recharge 5–6)	KEY:Creature ~ Storm Giant ~ Lightning Storm (Recharge 5–6)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Storm Giant Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Lightning Storm (Recharge 5–6)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.330	DESC:Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 18, each creature in a 10-foot-radius, 40-foot-high Cylinder originating from a point the giant can see within 500 feet. Failure: 55 (10d10) Lightning damage. Success: Half damage.
Storm Giant ~ Spellcasting	KEY:Creature ~ Storm Giant ~ Spellcasting	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Storm Giant Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Spellcasting	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.330	DESC:The giant casts one of the following spells, requiring no Material components and using Wisdom as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 18): At Will: Detect Magic , Light 1/Day: Control Weather
Succubus ~ Incubus Form	KEY:Creature ~ Succubus ~ Incubus Form	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Succubus Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Incubus Form	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.331	DESC:When the succubus finishes a Long Rest, it can shape-shift into an Incubus , using that stat block instead of this one.
Succubus ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Succubus ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Succubus Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.331	DESC:The succubus makes one Fiendish Touch attack and uses Charm or Draining Kiss.
Succubus ~ Fiendish Touch	KEY:Creature ~ Succubus ~ Fiendish Touch	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Succubus Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Fiendish Touch	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.331	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Psychic damage.
Succubus ~ Charm	KEY:Creature ~ Succubus ~ Charm	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Succubus Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Charm	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.331	DESC:The succubus casts Dominate Person (level 8 version), requiring no spell components and using Charisma as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 15).
Succubus ~ Draining Kiss	KEY:Creature ~ Succubus ~ Draining Kiss	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Succubus Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Draining Kiss	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.331	DESC:Constitution Saving Throw: DC 15, one creature Charmed by the succubus within 5 feet. Failure: 13 (3d8) Psychic damage. Success: Half damage. Failure or Success: The target’s Hit Point maximum decreases by an amount equal to the damage taken.
Succubus ~ Shape-Shift	KEY:Creature ~ Succubus ~ Shape-Shift	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Succubus Trait.MonsterBonusAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Shape-Shift	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.331	DESC:The succubus shape-shifts into a Medium or Small Humanoid, or it returns to its true form. Its game statistics are the same in each form, except its Fly Speed is available only in its true form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn’t transformed.
Tarrasque ~ Legendary Resistance (6/Day)	KEY:Creature ~ Tarrasque ~ Legendary Resistance (6/Day)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Tarrasque Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Legendary Resistance (6/Day)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.331	DESC:If the tarrasque fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.
Tarrasque ~ Magic Resistance	KEY:Creature ~ Tarrasque ~ Magic Resistance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Tarrasque Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Magic Resistance	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.331	DESC:The tarrasque has Advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.
Tarrasque ~ Reflective Carapace	KEY:Creature ~ Tarrasque ~ Reflective Carapace	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Tarrasque Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Reflective Carapace	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.331	DESC:If the tarrasque is targeted by a Magic Missile spell or a spell that requires a ranged attack roll, roll 1d6. On a 1–5 , the tarrasque is unaffected. On a 6 , the tarrasque is unaffected and reflects the spell, turning the caster into the target.
Tarrasque ~ Siege Monster	KEY:Creature ~ Tarrasque ~ Siege Monster	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Tarrasque Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Siege Monster	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.331	DESC:The tarrasque deals double damage to objects and structures.
Tarrasque ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Tarrasque ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Tarrasque Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.331	DESC:The tarrasque makes one Bite attack and three other attacks, using Claw or Tail in any combination.
Tarrasque ~ Bite	KEY:Creature ~ Tarrasque ~ Bite	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Tarrasque Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Bite	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.331	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +19, reach 15 ft. Hit: 36 (4d12 + 10) Piercing damage, and the target has the Grappled condition (escape DC 20). Until the grapple ends, the target has the Restrained condition and can’t teleport.
Tarrasque ~ Claw	KEY:Creature ~ Tarrasque ~ Claw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Tarrasque Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Claw	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.331	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +19, reach 15 ft. Hit: 28 (4d8 + 10) Slashing damage.
Tarrasque ~ Tail	KEY:Creature ~ Tarrasque ~ Tail	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Tarrasque Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Tail	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.331	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +19, reach 30 ft. Hit: 23 (3d8 + 10) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it has the Prone condition.
Tarrasque ~ Thunderous Bellow (Recharge 5–6)	KEY:Creature ~ Tarrasque ~ Thunderous Bellow (Recharge 5–6)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Tarrasque Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Thunderous Bellow (Recharge 5–6)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.331	DESC:Constitution Saving Throw: DC 27, each creature and each object that isn’t being worn or carried in a 150-foot Cone. Failure: 78 (12d12) Thunder damage, and the target has the Deafened and Frightened conditions until the end of its next turn. Success: Half damage only.
Tarrasque ~ Swallow	KEY:Creature ~ Tarrasque ~ Swallow	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Tarrasque Trait.MonsterBonusAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Swallow	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.331	DESC:Strength Saving Throw: DC 27, one Large or smaller creature Grappled by the tarrasque (it can have up to six creatures swallowed at a time). Failure: The target is swallowed, and the Grappled condition ends. A swallowed creature has the Blinded and Restrained conditions and can’t teleport, it has Total Cover against attacks and other effects outside the tarrasque, and it takes 56 (16d6) Acid damage at the start of each of the tarrasque’s turns. If the tarrasque takes 60 damage or more on a single turn from a creature inside it, the tarrasque must succeed on a DC 20 Constitution saving throw at the end of that turn or regurgitate all swallowed creatures, each of which falls in a space within 10 feet of the tarrasque and has the Prone condition. If the tarrasque dies, any swallowed creature no longer has the Restrained condition and can escape from the corpse using 20 feet of movement, exiting Prone.
Tarrasque ~ Onslaught	KEY:Creature ~ Tarrasque ~ Onslaught	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Tarrasque Trait.MonsterLegendaryAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Onslaught	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.331	DESC:The tarrasque moves up to half its Speed, and it makes one Claw or Tail attack.
Tarrasque ~ World-Shaking Movement	KEY:Creature ~ Tarrasque ~ World-Shaking Movement	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Tarrasque Trait.MonsterLegendaryAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:World-Shaking Movement	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.331	DESC:The tarrasque moves up to its Speed. At the end of this movement, the tarrasque creates an instantaneous shock wave in a 60-foot Emanation originating from itself. Creatures in that area lose Concentration and, if Medium or smaller, have the Prone condition. The tarrasque can’t take this action again until the start of its next turn.
Tough ~ Pack Tactics	KEY:Creature ~ Tough ~ Pack Tactics	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Tough Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Pack Tactics	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.332	DESC:The tough has Advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the tough’s allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally doesn’t have the Incapacitated condition.
Tough ~ Mace	KEY:Creature ~ Tough ~ Mace	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Tough Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Mace	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.332	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage.
Tough ~ Heavy Crossbow	KEY:Creature ~ Tough ~ Heavy Crossbow	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Tough Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Heavy Crossbow	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.332	DESC:Ranged Attack Roll: +3, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 6 (1d10 + 1) Piercing damage.
Tough Boss ~ Pack Tactics	KEY:Creature ~ Tough Boss ~ Pack Tactics	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Tough Boss Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Pack Tactics	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.332	DESC:The tough has Advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the tough’s allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally doesn’t have the Incapacitated condition.
Tough Boss ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Tough Boss ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Tough Boss Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.332	DESC:The tough makes two attacks, using Warhammer or Heavy Crossbow in any combination.
Tough Boss ~ Warhammer	KEY:Creature ~ Tough Boss ~ Warhammer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Tough Boss Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Warhammer	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.332	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, the tough pushes the target up to 10 feet straight away from itself.
Tough Boss ~ Heavy Crossbow	KEY:Creature ~ Tough Boss ~ Heavy Crossbow	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Tough Boss Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Heavy Crossbow	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.332	DESC:Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 13 (2d10 + 2) Piercing damage.
Treant ~ Siege Monster	KEY:Creature ~ Treant ~ Siege Monster	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Treant Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Siege Monster	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.333	DESC:The treant deals double damage to objects and structures.
Treant ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Treant ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Treant Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.333	DESC:The treant makes two Slam attacks.
Treant ~ Slam	KEY:Creature ~ Treant ~ Slam	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Treant Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Slam	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.333	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 5 ft. Hit: 16 (3d6 + 6) Bludgeoning damage.
Treant ~ Hail of Bark	KEY:Creature ~ Treant ~ Hail of Bark	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Treant Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Hail of Bark	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.333	DESC:Ranged Attack Roll: +10, range 180 ft. Hit: 28 (4d10 + 6) Piercing damage.
Treant ~ Animate Trees (1/Day)	KEY:Creature ~ Treant ~ Animate Trees (1/Day)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Treant Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Animate Trees (1/Day)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.333	DESC:The treant magically animates up to two trees it can see within 60 feet of itself. Each tree uses the Treant stat block, except it has Intelligence and Charisma scores of 1, it can’t speak, and it lacks this action. The tree takes its turn immediately after the treant on the same Initiative count, and it obeys the treant. A tree remains animate for 1 day or until it dies, the treant dies, or it is more than 120 feet from the treant. The tree then takes root if possible.
Troll ~ Loathsome Limbs (4/Day)	KEY:Creature ~ Troll ~ Loathsome Limbs (4/Day)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Troll Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Loathsome Limbs (4/Day)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.333	DESC:If the troll ends any turn Bloodied and took 15+ Slashing damage during that turn, one of the troll’s limbs is severed, falls into the troll’s space, and becomes a Troll Limb . The limb acts immediately after the troll’s turn. The troll has 1 Exhaustion level for each missing limb, and it grows replacement limbs the next time it regains Hit Points.
Troll ~ Regeneration	KEY:Creature ~ Troll ~ Regeneration	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Troll Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Regeneration	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.333	DESC:The troll regains 15 Hit Points at the start of each of its turns. If the troll takes Acid or Fire damage, this trait doesn’t function on the troll’s next turn. The troll dies only if it starts its turn with 0 Hit Points and doesn’t regenerate.
Troll ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Troll ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Troll Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.333	DESC:The troll makes three Rend attacks.
Troll ~ Rend	KEY:Creature ~ Troll ~ Rend	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Troll Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Rend	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.333	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage.
Troll ~ Charge	KEY:Creature ~ Troll ~ Charge	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Troll Trait.MonsterBonusAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Charge	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.333	DESC:The troll moves up to half its Speed straight toward an enemy it can see.
Troll Limb ~ Regeneration	KEY:Creature ~ Troll Limb ~ Regeneration	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Troll Limb Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Regeneration	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.333	DESC:The limb regains 5 Hit Points at the start of each of its turns. If the limb takes Acid or Fire damage, this trait doesn’t function on the limb’s next turn. The limb dies only if it starts its turn with 0 Hit Points and doesn’t regenerate.
Troll Limb ~ Troll Spawn	KEY:Creature ~ Troll Limb ~ Troll Spawn	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Troll Limb Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Troll Spawn	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.333	DESC:The limb uncannily has the same senses as a whole troll. If the limb isn’t destroyed within 24 hours, roll 1d12. On a 12, the limb turns into a Troll . Otherwise, the limb withers away.
Troll Limb ~ Rend	KEY:Creature ~ Troll Limb ~ Rend	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Troll Limb Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Rend	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.333	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d4 + 4) Slashing damage.
Unicorn ~ Legendary Resistance (3/Day)	KEY:Creature ~ Unicorn ~ Legendary Resistance (3/Day)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Unicorn Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Legendary Resistance (3/Day)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:If the unicorn fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.
Unicorn ~ Magic Resistance	KEY:Creature ~ Unicorn ~ Magic Resistance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Unicorn Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Magic Resistance	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:The unicorn has Advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.
Unicorn ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Unicorn ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Unicorn Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:The unicorn makes one Hooves attack and one Radiant Horn attack.
Unicorn ~ Hooves	KEY:Creature ~ Unicorn ~ Hooves	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Unicorn Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Hooves	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage.
Unicorn ~ Radiant Horn	KEY:Creature ~ Unicorn ~ Radiant Horn	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Unicorn Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Radiant Horn	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d10 + 4) Radiant damage.
Unicorn ~ Spellcasting	KEY:Creature ~ Unicorn ~ Spellcasting	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Unicorn Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Spellcasting	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:The unicorn casts one of the following spells, requiring no spell components and using Charisma as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 14): At Will: Detect Evil and Good , Druidcraft 1/Day Each: Calm Emotions , Dispel Evil and Good , Entangle , Pass without Trace , Word of Recall
Unicorn ~ Unicorn’s Blessing (3/Day)	KEY:Creature ~ Unicorn ~ Unicorn’s Blessing (3/Day)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Unicorn Trait.MonsterBonusAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Unicorn’s Blessing (3/Day)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:The unicorn touches another creature with its horn and casts Cure Wounds or Lesser Restoration on that creature, using the same spellcasting ability as Spellcasting.
Unicorn ~ Charging Horn	KEY:Creature ~ Unicorn ~ Charging Horn	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Unicorn Trait.MonsterLegendaryAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Charging Horn	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:The unicorn moves up to half its Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks, and it makes one Radiant Horn attack.
Unicorn ~ Shimmering Shield	KEY:Creature ~ Unicorn ~ Shimmering Shield	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Unicorn Trait.MonsterLegendaryAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Shimmering Shield	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:The unicorn targets itself or one creature it can see within 60 feet of itself. The target gains 10 (3d6) Temporary Hit Points, and its AC increases by 2 until the end of the unicorn’s next turn. The unicorn can’t take this action again until the start of its next turn.
Vampire Familiar ~ Vampiric Connection	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire Familiar ~ Vampiric Connection	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Familiar Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Vampiric Connection	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:While the familiar and its vampire master are on the same plane of existence, the vampire can communicate with the familiar telepathically, and the vampire can perceive through the familiar’s senses.
Vampire Familiar ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire Familiar ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Familiar Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:The familiar makes two Umbral Dagger attacks.
Vampire Familiar ~ Umbral Dagger	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire Familiar ~ Umbral Dagger	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Familiar Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Umbral Dagger	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Piercing damage plus 7 (3d4) Necrotic damage. If the target is reduced to 0 Hit Points by this attack, the target becomes Stable but has the Poisoned condition for 1 hour. While it has the Poisoned condition, the target has the Paralyzed condition.
Vampire Familiar ~ Deathless Agility	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire Familiar ~ Deathless Agility	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Familiar Trait.MonsterBonusAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Deathless Agility	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:The familiar takes the Dash or Disengage action.
Vampire Spawn ~ Spider Climb	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire Spawn ~ Spider Climb	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Spawn Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Spider Climb	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:The vampire can climb difficult surfaces, including along ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.
Vampire Spawn ~ Vampire Weakness	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire Spawn ~ Vampire Weakness	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Spawn Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Vampire Weakness	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:The vampire has these weaknesses: Forbiddance. The vampire can’t enter a residence without an invitation from an occupant.
Vampire Spawn ~ Running Water	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire Spawn ~ Running Water	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Spawn Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Running Water	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:The vampire takes 20 Acid damage if it ends its turn in running water. Stake to the Heart. The vampire is destroyed if a weapon that deals Piercing damage is driven into the vampire’s heart while the vampire has the Incapacitated condition.
Vampire Spawn ~ Sunlight	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire Spawn ~ Sunlight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Spawn Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Sunlight	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:The vampire takes 20 Radiant damage if it starts its turn in sunlight. While in sunlight, it has Disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks.
Vampire Spawn ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire Spawn ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Spawn Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:The vampire makes two Claw attacks and uses Bite.
Vampire Spawn ~ Claw	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire Spawn ~ Claw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Spawn Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Claw	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d4 + 3) Slashing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the Grappled condition (escape DC 13) from one of two claws.
Vampire Spawn ~ Bite	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire Spawn ~ Bite	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Spawn Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Bite	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:Constitution Saving Throw: DC 14, one creature within 5 feet that is willing or that has the Grappled, Incapacitated, or Restrained condition. Failure: 5 (1d4 + 3) Piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage. The target’s Hit Point maximum decreases by an amount equal to the Necrotic damage taken, and the vampire regains Hit Points equal to that amount.
Vampire Spawn ~ Deathless Agility	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire Spawn ~ Deathless Agility	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Spawn Trait.MonsterBonusAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Deathless Agility	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.334	DESC:The vampire takes the Dash or Disengage action.
Vampire ~ Misty Escape	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire ~ Misty Escape	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Misty Escape	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.335	DESC:If the vampire drops to 0 Hit Points outside its resting place, the vampire uses Shape-Shift to become mist (no action required). If it can’t use ShapeShift, it is destroyed. While it has 0 Hit Points in mist form, it can’t return to its vampire form, and it must reach its resting place within 2 hours or be destroyed. Once in its resting place, it returns to its vampire form and has the Paralyzed condition until it regains any Hit Points, and it regains 1 Hit Point after spending 1 hour there.
Vampire ~ Spider Climb	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire ~ Spider Climb	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Spider Climb	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.335	DESC:The vampire can climb difficult surfaces, including along ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.
Vampire ~ Vampire Weakness	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire ~ Vampire Weakness	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Vampire Weakness	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.335	DESC:The vampire has these weaknesses: Forbiddance. The vampire can’t enter a residence without an invitation from an occupant.
Vampire ~ Running Water	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire ~ Running Water	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Running Water	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.335	DESC:The vampire takes 20 Acid damage if it ends its turn in running water. Stake to the Heart. If a weapon that deals Piercing damage is driven into the vampire’s heart while the vampire has the Incapacitated condition in its resting place, the vampire has the Paralyzed condition until the weapon is removed.
Vampire ~ Sunlight	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire ~ Sunlight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Sunlight	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.335	DESC:The vampire takes 20 Radiant damage if it starts its turn in sunlight. While in sunlight, it has Disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks.
Vampire ~ Multiattack (Vampire Form Only)	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire ~ Multiattack (Vampire Form Only)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack (Vampire Form Only)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.335	DESC:The vampire makes two Grave Strike attacks and uses Bite.
Vampire ~ Grave Strike (Vampire Form Only)	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire ~ Grave Strike (Vampire Form Only)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Grave Strike (Vampire Form Only)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.335	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the Grappled condition (escape DC 14) from one of two hands.
Vampire ~ Bite (Bat or Vampire Form Only)	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire ~ Bite (Bat or Vampire Form Only)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Bite (Bat or Vampire Form Only)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.335	DESC:Constitution Saving Throw: DC 17, one creature within 5 feet that is willing or that has the Grappled, Incapacitated, or Restrained condition. Failure: 6 (1d4 + 4) Piercing damage plus 13 (3d8) Necrotic damage. The target’s Hit Point maximum decreases by an amount equal to the Necrotic damage taken, and the vampire regains Hit Points equal to that amount. A Humanoid reduced to 0 Hit Points by this damage and then buried rises the following sunset as a Vampire Spawn under the vampire’s control.
Vampire ~ Charm (Recharge 5–6)	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire ~ Charm (Recharge 5–6)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Trait.MonsterBonusAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Charm (Recharge 5–6)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.335	DESC:The vampire casts Charm Person , requiring no spell components and using Charisma as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 17), and the duration is 24 hours. The Charmed target is a willing recipient of the vampire’s Bite, the damage of which doesn’t end the spell. When the spell ends, the target is unaware it was Charmed by the vampire.
Vampire ~ Shape-Shift	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire ~ Shape-Shift	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Trait.MonsterBonusAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Shape-Shift	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.335	DESC:If the vampire isn’t in sunlight or running water, it shape-shifts into a Tiny bat (Speed 5 ft., Fly Speed 30 ft.) or a Medium cloud of mist (Speed 5 ft., Fly Speed 20 ft. [hover]), or it returns to its vampire form. Anything it is wearing transforms with it. While in bat form, the vampire can’t speak. Its game statistics, other than its size and Speed, are unchanged. While in mist form, the vampire can’t take any actions, speak, or manipulate objects. It is weightless and can enter an enemy’s space and stop there. If air can pass through a space, the mist can do so, but it can’t pass through liquid. It has Resistance to all damage, except the damage it takes from sunlight.
Vampire ~ Beguile	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire ~ Beguile	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Trait.MonsterLegendaryAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Beguile	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.335	DESC:The vampire casts Command , requiring no spell components and using Charisma as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 17). The vampire can’t take this action again until the start of its next turn.
Vampire ~ Deathless Strike	KEY:Creature ~ Vampire ~ Deathless Strike	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vampire Trait.MonsterLegendaryAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Deathless Strike	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.335	DESC:The vampire moves up to half its Speed, and it makes one Grave Strike attack.
Vrock ~ Demonic Restoration	KEY:Creature ~ Vrock ~ Demonic Restoration	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vrock Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Demonic Restoration	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.336	DESC:If the vrock dies outside the Abyss, its body dissolves into ichor, and it gains a new body instantly, reviving with all its Hit Points somewhere in the Abyss.
Vrock ~ Magic Resistance	KEY:Creature ~ Vrock ~ Magic Resistance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vrock Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Magic Resistance	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.336	DESC:The vrock has Advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.
Vrock ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Vrock ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vrock Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.336	DESC:The vrock makes two Shred attacks.
Vrock ~ Shred	KEY:Creature ~ Vrock ~ Shred	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vrock Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Shred	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.336	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) Poison damage.
Vrock ~ Spores (Recharge 6)	KEY:Creature ~ Vrock ~ Spores (Recharge 6)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vrock Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Spores (Recharge 6)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.336	DESC:Constitution Saving Throw: DC 15, each creature in a 20-foot Emanation originating from the vrock. Failure: The target has the Poisoned condition and repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. While Poisoned, the target takes 5 (1d10) Poison damage at the start of each of its turns. Emptying a flask of Holy Water on the target ends the effect early.
Vrock ~ Stunning Screech (1/Day)	KEY:Creature ~ Vrock ~ Stunning Screech (1/Day)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Vrock Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Stunning Screech (1/Day)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.336	DESC:Constitution Saving Throw: DC 15, each creature in a 20-foot Emanation originating from the vrock (demons succeed automatically). Failure: 10 (3d6) Thunder damage, and the target has the Stunned condition until the end of the vrock’s next turn.
Warrior Infantry ~ Pack Tactics	KEY:Creature ~ Warrior Infantry ~ Pack Tactics	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Warrior Infantry Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Pack Tactics	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.336	DESC:The warrior has Advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the warrior’s allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally doesn’t have the Incapacitated condition.
Warrior Infantry ~ Spear	KEY:Creature ~ Warrior Infantry ~ Spear	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Warrior Infantry Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Spear	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.336	DESC:Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage.
Warrior Veteran ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Warrior Veteran ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Warrior Veteran Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.337	DESC:The warrior makes two Greatsword or Heavy Crossbow attacks.
Warrior Veteran ~ Greatsword	KEY:Creature ~ Warrior Veteran ~ Greatsword	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Warrior Veteran Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Greatsword	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.337	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage.
Warrior Veteran ~ Heavy Crossbow	KEY:Creature ~ Warrior Veteran ~ Heavy Crossbow	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Warrior Veteran Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Heavy Crossbow	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.337	DESC:Ranged Attack Roll: +3, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 12 (2d10 + 1) Piercing damage.
Warrior Veteran ~ Parry	KEY:Creature ~ Warrior Veteran ~ Parry	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Warrior Veteran Trait.MonsterReaction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Parry	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.337	DESC:Trigger: The warrior is hit by a melee attack roll while holding a weapon. Response: The warrior adds 2 to its AC against that attack, possibly causing it to miss.
Water Elemental ~ Freeze	KEY:Creature ~ Water Elemental ~ Freeze	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Water Elemental Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Freeze	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.337	DESC:If the elemental takes Cold damage, its Speed decreases by 20 feet until the end of its next turn.
Water Elemental ~ Water Form	KEY:Creature ~ Water Elemental ~ Water Form	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Water Elemental Trait.MonsterTrait.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Water Form	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.337	DESC:The elemental can enter an enemy’s space and stop there. It can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch without expending extra movement to do so.
Water Elemental ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Water Elemental ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Water Elemental Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.337	DESC:The elemental makes two Slam attacks.
Water Elemental ~ Slam	KEY:Creature ~ Water Elemental ~ Slam	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Water Elemental Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Slam	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.337	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the Prone condition.
Water Elemental ~ Whelm (Recharge 4–6)	KEY:Creature ~ Water Elemental ~ Whelm (Recharge 4–6)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Water Elemental Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Whelm (Recharge 4–6)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.337	DESC:Strength Saving Throw: DC 15, each creature in the elemental’s space. Failure: 22 (4d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the Grappled condition (escape DC 14). Until the grapple ends, the target has the Restrained condition, is suffocating unless it can breathe water, and takes 9 (2d8) Bludgeoning damage at the start of each of the elemental’s turns. The elemental can grapple one Large creature or up to two Medium or smaller creatures at a time with Whelm. As an action, a creature within 5 feet of the elemental can pull a creature out of it by succeeding on a DC 14 Strength (Athletics) check. Success: Half damage only.
Werebear ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Werebear ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Werebear Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.337	DESC:The werebear makes two attacks, using Handaxe or Rend in any combination. It can replace one attack with a Bite attack.
Werebear ~ Bite (Bear or Hybrid Form Only)	KEY:Creature ~ Werebear ~ Bite (Bear or Hybrid Form Only)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Werebear Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Bite (Bear or Hybrid Form Only)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.337	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 17 (2d12 + 4) Piercing damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it is subjected to the following effect. Constitution Saving Throw: DC 14. Failure: The target is cursed. If the cursed target drops to 0 Hit Points, it instead becomes a Werebear under the GM’s control and has 10 Hit Points. Success: The target is immune to this werebear’s curse for 24 hours.
Werebear ~ Handaxe (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)	KEY:Creature ~ Werebear ~ Handaxe (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Werebear Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Handaxe (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.337	DESC:Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 14 (3d6 + 4) Slashing damage.
Werebear ~ Rend (Bear or Hybrid Form Only)	KEY:Creature ~ Werebear ~ Rend (Bear or Hybrid Form Only)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Werebear Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Rend (Bear or Hybrid Form Only)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.337	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Slashing damage.
Werebear ~ Shape-Shift	KEY:Creature ~ Werebear ~ Shape-Shift	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Werebear Trait.MonsterBonusAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Shape-Shift	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.337	DESC:The werebear shape-shifts into a Large bear-humanoid hybrid form or a Large bear, or it returns to its true humanoid form. Its game statistics, other than its size, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn’t transformed.
Wereboar ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Wereboar ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Wereboar Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.338	DESC:The wereboar makes two attacks, using Javelin or Tusk in any combination. It can replace one attack with a Gore attack.
Wereboar ~ Gore (Boar or Hybrid Form Only)	KEY:Creature ~ Wereboar ~ Gore (Boar or Hybrid Form Only)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Wereboar Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Gore (Boar or Hybrid Form Only)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.338	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Piercing damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it is subjected to the following effect. Constitution Saving Throw: DC 12. Failure: The target is cursed. If the cursed target drops to 0 Hit Points, it instead becomes a Wereboar under the GM’s control and has 10 Hit Points. Success: The target is immune to this wereboar’s curse for 24 hours.
Wereboar ~ Javelin (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)	KEY:Creature ~ Wereboar ~ Javelin (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Wereboar Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Javelin (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.338	DESC:Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 13 (3d6 + 3) Piercing damage.
Wereboar ~ Tusk (Boar or Hybrid Form Only)	KEY:Creature ~ Wereboar ~ Tusk (Boar or Hybrid Form Only)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Wereboar Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Tusk (Boar or Hybrid Form Only)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.338	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature and the wereboar moved 20+ feet straight toward it immediately before the hit, the target takes an extra 7 (2d6) Piercing damage and has the Prone condition.
Wereboar ~ Shape-Shift	KEY:Creature ~ Wereboar ~ Shape-Shift	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Wereboar Trait.MonsterBonusAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Shape-Shift	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.338	DESC:The wereboar shape-shifts into a Medium boar-humanoid hybrid or a Small boar, or it returns to its true humanoid form. Its game statistics, other than its size, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn’t transformed.
Wererat ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Wererat ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Wererat Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.338	DESC:The wererat makes two attacks, using Scratch or Hand Crossbow in any combination. It can replace one attack with a Bite attack.
Wererat ~ Bite (Rat or Hybrid Form Only)	KEY:Creature ~ Wererat ~ Bite (Rat or Hybrid Form Only)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Wererat Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Bite (Rat or Hybrid Form Only)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.338	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d4 + 3) Piercing damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it is subjected to the following effect. Constitution Saving Throw: DC 11. Failure: The target is cursed. If the cursed target drops to 0 Hit Points, it instead becomes a Wererat under the GM’s control and has 10 Hit Points. Success: The target is immune to this wererat’s curse for 24 hours.
Wererat ~ Scratch	KEY:Creature ~ Wererat ~ Scratch	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Wererat Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Scratch	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.338	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Slashing damage. Hand Crossbow (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only). Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage.
Wererat ~ Shape-Shift	KEY:Creature ~ Wererat ~ Shape-Shift	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Wererat Trait.MonsterBonusAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Shape-Shift	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.338	DESC:The wererat shape-shifts into a Medium rat-humanoid hybrid or a Small rat, or it returns to its true humanoid form. Its game statistics, other than its size, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn’t transformed.
Weretiger ~ Multiattack	KEY:Creature ~ Weretiger ~ Multiattack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Weretiger Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Multiattack	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.339	DESC:The weretiger makes two attacks, using Scratch or Longbow in any combination. It can replace one attack with a Bite attack.
Weretiger ~ Bite (Tiger or Hybrid Form Only)	KEY:Creature ~ Weretiger ~ Bite (Tiger or Hybrid Form Only)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Weretiger Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Bite (Tiger or Hybrid Form Only)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.339	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Piercing damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it is subjected to the following effect. Constitution Saving Throw: DC 13. Failure: The target is cursed. If the cursed target drops to 0 Hit Points, it instead becomes a Weretiger under the GM’s control and has 10 Hit Points. Success: The target is immune to this weretiger’s curse for 24 hours.
Weretiger ~ Scratch	KEY:Creature ~ Weretiger ~ Scratch	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Weretiger Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Scratch	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.339	DESC:Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage.
Weretiger ~ Longbow (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)	KEY:Creature ~ Weretiger ~ Longbow (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Weretiger Trait.MonsterAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Longbow (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.339	DESC:Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 11 (2d8 + 2) Piercing damage.
Weretiger ~ Prowl (Tiger or Hybrid Form Only)	KEY:Creature ~ Weretiger ~ Prowl (Tiger or Hybrid Form Only)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Weretiger Trait.MonsterBonusAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Prowl (Tiger or Hybrid Form Only)	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.339	DESC:The weretiger moves up to its Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks. At the end of this movement, the weretiger can take the Hide action.
Weretiger ~ Shape-Shift	KEY:Creature ~ Weretiger ~ Shape-Shift	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Weretiger Trait.MonsterBonusAction.SpecialQuality.Race Trait	OUTPUTNAME:Shape-Shift	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.339	DESC:The weretiger shape-shifts into a Large tiger-humanoid hybrid or a Large tiger, or it returns to its true humanoid form. Its game statistics, other than its size, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn’t transformed.
